  "canonical_schema_boundary": [
    "Current F16 data/schema/traits.json and traits.schema.json admit only hardy/max_hp_scale.",
    "canonical_catalog preserves that exact row; candidate_catalog uses the same literal four-field row shape and labels all 29 other identities as proposals.",
    "Do not pass the full config envelope to RedesignData.load_catalog: F16 expects an array. The helper validates only source canonical_catalog through F16 and validates disabled proposals separately.",
    "The new config envelope is a draft extension, not an already registered F16 schema. Do not call the full candidate pool canonical until the authorized writer extends traits manifest/schema and character trait enums coherently."
  ],
  "host_boundary": [
    "preview_roll requires seven HOST-sampled [0,1) draws and host-owned alpha/night/weather spawn facts; the module creates no RNG and admits no network request.",
    "Both typed result containers and every typed effect proposal carry admissible=false; code=draft_only indicates content preview, never gameplay authorization.",
    "preview_effects emits one scalar target with an eligibility gate per distinct id; all inputs and output proposals are detached, with no stat application.",
    "No grant of swim/fly/climb permission, no trainer damage, no held gameplay input, no producer/automation behavior and no ownership-cap change.",
    "Future Session must recompute from its admitted canonical record, sample RNG only on the host and stage its existing personalized character ledger before same-record CAS.",
    "Release must atomically combine existing release:<uid> receipts, chosen seed, essence, inventory capacity and owned uid removal; no second roster/receipt store.",
    "Teach must require completed breakthrough, slot, canonical seed payload and species-derived essence; overwrite destroys the old taught trait, with duplicate checks across all admitted visible traits."
  ],
  "unresolved_proposals": [
    "Existing TRAINING section 12 item 4: personality mapping remains OFF; existing primary/hidden secondary identity and current bond threshold are preserved. No capacity/duplicate resolution is silently chosen.",
    "Dual-type teaching debit has no explicit settled rule; primary-type debit is labeled a disabled proposal pending training-owner review.",
    "Strongest eligible magnitude per scalar target/event replaces the earlier multiplicative stacking proposal. It remains disabled pending COMBAT formula order/caps/network review; no new hard rule has been adopted.",
    "Rare traversal/projectile/stagger consumers need real-path review; content does not prove those hooks exist.",
    "Trait Seed item identity/payload/stacking must be registered by ItemDB owner. No made-up generic seed item id is treated as usable inventory."
  ],
  "content_refinements": [
    "Canonical hardy/common/max_hp_scale/0.05 appears unchanged in both canonical_catalog and candidate_catalog.",
    "The eight existing Common personality effects keep the exact CREATURES section 3.1 scalar targets and 5% magnitudes; mapping remains disabled.",
    "All 30 candidate ids and effect ids are distinct; counts remain Common12/Rare10/Epic8 and every magnitude respects its 5/8/12% cap.",
    "The eight Epic type-power rows share a scalar family but have distinct mutually exclusive host move-type gates; no generic Epic power row is added.",
    "Typed effects expose scalar_target_group and the pending strongest-eligible proposal so a future consumer cannot mistake distinct ids for permission to multiply overlapping power effects.",
    "Keen Aim preserves projectile range, Far Reach preserves projectile speed, Watchful preserves Burst distance/timing/vulnerability and Surefoot explicitly applies outside combat.",
    "The earlier multiplicative proposal could produce a 17.6% charged-fire bonus from Bold5% and Flameheart12%; the disabled strongest-eligible proposal would leave that target at12%."
  ],
  "integration_next": [
    "Re-read and compare source hashes before adopting; another lane can change the base while this helper stays read-only.",
    "Adopt only the two proposed NEW paths after reviewing the exact patch. Do not replace existing data/traits/traits.json or trait_db.gd.",
    "Complete canonical registry additions and settle identity mapping separately; remove draft-only restrictions only in a reviewed operational implementation.",
    "Keep all F30 criteria OPEN until named per-trait effects, roll distribution, persistence, UI and host transaction proofs are produced by the owning lane."
